      "content": "If the world has already decided who you are, then fighting that narrative is just exhausting yourself for no reward. It's a heavy, suffocating weight to carry the pre-judgment of strangers. Instead of fighting the inevitable, maybe you could just stop trying to prove anything to them. A small, quiet act of self-caring, something that only benefits *you*, could be a start toward making the emptiness feel a little less absolute.",
